GN[the milk tea game]PW[spaceandgames]PB[lindentree]WR[2d]BR[2d]DT[2020-10-25]PC[OGS: https://online-go.com/game/27803367]C[Thoughts on improving:

If we can correct 13 points of mistakes in our gameplay, that should be enough to gain 1 stone in strength (because 1 handicap stone = about 13 points).

We can begin with faith in KataGo's judgments. However, that doesn't mean we should always try to mimic KataGo's favorite move. Other considerations are:

(1) We may choose to study moves that are relatively easy for us to understand and remember
(2) We may choose moves that would tend to confuse our opponents

However, for the most part I think we should try to maximize the accuracy of our moves.

I think that:
(1) In the endgame, we should aim to play the very best moves.
(2) in the opening, we should aim to play the best moves that are consistent with our style preferences
(3) in the midgame, we should aim to reduce our mistakes by 50%.

In the midgame, the best move might be very hard to understand. However, if the move we played lost 6 points, and there's a different move that only loses 3 points, but which we are able to understand, then we should study that move so we can use it the next time we're in a similar situation.


Some new proverbs:
1. The knight's triangle is a good shape.
2. Be aware of peeping points.
3. Check for profitable moves before running.]RE[W+12.50]
